<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pharnavazid dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pharnavazid dynasty was the first royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> (Kartli) in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> according to Georgian tradition, named after its founder Pharnavaz I, who is credited with uniting the kingdom around 300 BCE. Its kings ruled, with interruptions, into the early centuries CE, but the dynastic lists preserved in the medieval chronicle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kartlis-tskhovreba">Kartlis Tskhovreba</a> are partly legendary.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pharnavazid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Pharnavazid dynasty" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julianna Lees · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:State_Museum_of_History_of_Georgia_(Tbilisi_Archaeological_Museum)_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
